<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Feb producer price index up 9.3 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>S.African Feb producer price index up 9.3 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's all-commodities producer price index rose 0.4 percent in February from January after rising 0.8 percent in January, Central Statistical Service figures show.</p>
<p>The year-on-year rise in February was 9.3 percent after January's 9.2 percent rise.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast PPI would rise 0.7 percent month-on-month and 9.5 percent year-on-year.  </p>
<p>    Pct changes:	     Year/year		    month/month</p>
<p>			 Feb'97   Jan'97   Feb'96  - latest   prev</p>
<p>All commodities     9.3	9.2     6.3	    0.4	0.8</p>
<p>Locally produced    9.2	9.2     6.7	    0.4	0.9</p>
<p>Imported	     10.3	9.6     5.2	    1.0	0.6</p>
<p>Index (base 1995=100):</p>
<p>			 Feb'97    Jan'97    Feb'96</p>
<p>All commodities    112.8     112.3     103.2</p>
<p>Locally produced   113.3     112.9     103.8</p>
<p>Imported	     111.8     110.7     101.4</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
